($q$Nkabom Collaborative PhD Scholarship at KNUST$q$,$q$Nkabom Collaborative (KNUST)$q$,$q$Ghana$q$,$q$Not stated$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$3-year full-time PhD research scholarship at KNUST in food systems, nutrition, entrepreneurship and packaging. Needs an MSc or MPhil with a research thesis, and admission to a KNUST PhD. Partner schools: KNUST.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://www.knust.edu.gh/announcements/general/call-applications-phd-scholarship-nkabom-collaborative$q$,$q$3-year PhD research scholarship, benefits not itemised$q$),
($q$DAAD Study Scholarships for STEM Disciplines for Ghanaians$q$,$q$DAAD (German Academic Exchange Service)$q$,$q$Germany$q$,$q$Not stated$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$For high-achieving students from developing and emerging countries with a first degree recognised in Germany. Covers a full-time on-campus Master's in maths, computer science, natural sciences or engineering at a German state or state-recognised university. People who already hold a Master's cannot apply.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://www.daad-ghana.org/en/find-funding/masters-degree/$q$,$q$Master's study in Germany; amounts not stated on the page$q$),
($q$DAAD Development-Related Postgraduate Courses (EPOS)$q$,$q$DAAD (German Academic Exchange Service)$q$,$q$Germany$q$,$q$Not stated$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$For graduates with at least a Second Class Upper degree, at least two years of relevant work experience, and a degree earned within the last six years. 12 to 24 month Master's courses for professionals focused on developing countries. Apply directly to the host university.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://www.daad-ghana.org/en/find-funding/masters-degree/$q$,$q$Scholarship for Master's course in Germany; amounts not stated on the page$q$),
($q$Helmut-Schmidt Programme (Public Policy and Good Governance)$q$,$q$DAAD (German Academic Exchange Service)$q$,$q$Germany$q$,$q$Not stated$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$For well-qualified graduates with a first university degree who want to contribute to their home country's social and economic development. Two-year Master's in public policy, good governance, international relations, public management and similar fields. Apply through the chosen course.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://www.daad-ghana.org/en/find-funding/masters-degree/$q$,$q$Scholarship for a two-year Master's in Germany; amounts not stated on the page$q$),
($q$DAAD Study Scholarships for Foreign Graduates in Music, Performing Arts, Fine Art, Design and Film$q$,$q$DAAD (German Academic Exchange Service)$q$,$q$Germany$q$,$q$Not stated$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$For foreign graduates with a Bachelor's degree in the relevant art field. Funds a Master's or a complementary course at a German state or state-recognised university.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://www.daad-ghana.org/en/find-funding/masters-degree/$q$,$q$Scholarship for study in Germany; amounts not stated on the page$q$),
($q$DAAD Study Scholarships for Foreign Graduates in Architecture$q$,$q$DAAD (German Academic Exchange Service)$q$,$q$Germany$q$,$q$Not stated$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$For foreign graduates in architecture with a Bachelor's degree. Funds a Master's or complementary study at a German state or state-recognised university.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://www.daad-ghana.org/en/find-funding/other-scholarships/$q$,$q$Scholarship for study in Germany; amounts not stated on the page$q$),
($q$DAAD In-Country/In-Region Scholarship Programme$q$,$q$DAAD (German Academic Exchange Service)$q$,$q$Africa (university outside home country)$q$,$q$Not stated$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$Funds Master's or PhD study at an African university outside your home country, for students from Sub-Saharan Africa. Apply first to the partner African network, which nominates candidates. DAAD does not take direct applications.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://www.daad-ghana.org/en/find-funding/other-scholarships/$q$,$q$Master's or PhD study at a partner African university$q$),
($q$DAAD African Centres of Excellence Scholarships$q$,$q$DAAD (German Academic Exchange Service)$q$,$q$Ghana$q$,$q$Not stated$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$Individual Master's and PhD scholarships at DAAD-funded centres at leading African universities, two of which are in Ghana. Apply directly to the centre, not to DAAD head office. Partner schools: University of Ghana (WACCI, RIPS), University for Development Studies.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://www.daad-ghana.org/en/find-funding/other-scholarships/$q$,$q$Master's or PhD scholarship at a centre of excellence$q$),
($q$Konrad-Adenauer-Stiftung Scholarships for International Students$q$,$q$Konrad-Adenauer-Stiftung$q$,$q$Germany$q$,$q$Partial$q$,$q$Undergraduate and postgraduate$q$,$q$For international (non-EU) students and doctoral candidates at German universities. Needs German at B2, strong grades, and commitment to democracy and human rights. Master's applicants must join a four-semester MA programme in Germany. Medicine and dentistry state exam programmes are not funded.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://www.kas.de/en/web/begabtenfoerderung-und-kultur/international-talent-development$q$,$q$Up to EUR 992 a month (Bachelor's and Master's) or up to EUR 1,400 a month (doctoral), plus optional extras$q$),
($q$Heinrich Boell Foundation Scholarships for International Graduate and Doctoral Students$q$,$q$Heinrich Boell Foundation$q$,$q$Germany$q$,$q$Partial$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$For international graduates with a first degree who want to do a Master's or PhD in Germany. Special consideration for students from the global south. Needs German at B2 or DSH II. Selection looks at grades, civic engagement and political interest.$q$,'2027-03-01'::date,$q$https://www.boell.de/en/scholarships$q$,$q$Maintenance grant plus study, mobility and family allowances; amounts not stated on the page$q$),
($q$Stipendium Hungaricum Scholarship (Ghana)$q$,$q$Government of Hungary (Tempus Public Foundation)$q$,$q$Hungary$q$,$q$Full$q$,$q$Undergraduate and postgraduate$q$,$q$For Ghanaian citizens resident in Ghana, applied for through the Ghana Scholarships Secretariat. Undergraduate: WASSCE aggregate 6 to 15, age 23 or under. Master's and PhD: 2nd Class Upper or better, 2 years of work experience, national service done, age 35 or under (Master's) or 45 or under (PhD).$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://scholarships.gov.gh/opportunities/offer-of-scholarships-by-the-government-of-hungary-under-the-educational-exchange-programme-tenable-in-hungary$q$,$q$Tuition-free study, monthly stipend, accommodation contribution, medical insurance$q$),
($q$Turkiye Burslari (Turkiye Scholarships)$q$,$q$Government of Turkiye (Presidency for Turks Abroad and Related Communities)$q$,$q$Turkey$q$,$q$Full$q$,$q$Undergraduate and postgraduate$q$,$q$Open to international students from all countries for associate, bachelor's, master's and doctoral study at Turkish universities. The 2026 window ran 10 January to 20 February 2026.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://turkiyeburslari.gov.tr/duyurular/turkiye-burslari-2026-basvurulari-121$q$,$q$Tuition, accommodation, health insurance and financial support$q$),
($q$Chinese Government Scholarship for Ghanaian Students$q$,$q$Government of China (China Scholarship Council) via Ghana Scholarships Authority$q$,$q$China$q$,$q$Not stated$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$For Ghanaian citizens resident in Ghana. Master's: at least Second Class Upper, age 35 or under. PhD: Second Class Upper plus a relevant Master's, age 40 or under. Apply online to the China Scholarship Council and send documents to the Ghana Scholarships Secretariat.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://scholarships.gov.gh/opportunities/chinese-government-scholarship-awards-to-ghanaian-students-for-20262027-academic-year$q$,$q$Benefits not described on the notice$q$),
($q$Japanese Government (MEXT) Scholarship for Ghana: Research Students$q$,$q$Government of Japan (MEXT) via Embassy of Japan in Ghana$q$,$q$Japan$q$,$q$Full$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$For Ghanaian citizens born on or after 2 April 1992 who are willing to learn Japanese. Master's or doctoral research at a Japanese graduate school, 18 months to 2 years including 6 months of Japanese study.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://www.gh.emb-japan.go.jp/itpr_ja/11_000001_00538.html$q$,$q$Tuition waived, monthly allowance of about 144,000 to 145,000 yen, airfare to Japan$q$),
($q$Eiffel Excellence Scholarship Programme$q$,$q$French Ministry for Europe and Foreign Affairs (run by Campus France)$q$,$q$France$q$,$q$Not stated$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$For foreign students under 29 (Master's) or under 35 (PhD), in priority fields. Only French higher education institutions can submit applications, so apply through the institution you want to join. No excluded countries are listed on the page.$q$,'2027-01-06'::date,$q$https://campusfrance.org/en/eiffel-scholarship-program-of-excellence$q$,$q$Benefits not described on the page$q$),
($q$Erasmus Mundus Joint Masters Scholarships$q$,$q$European Commission (Erasmus+)$q$,$q$Europe (several countries)$q$,$q$Full$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$Students from all over the world with a Bachelor's degree (or in final year) can apply directly to a joint Master's programme run by universities in at least two European countries. Check each programme for its deadline.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://erasmus-plus.ec.europa.eu/opportunities/individuals/students/erasmus-mundus-joint-masters$q$,$q$Covers participation costs, with a contribution to travel, visa and living allowance for awarded students$q$),
($q$Government of Ireland International Education Scholarships$q$,$q$Government of Ireland (Higher Education Authority)$q$,$q$Ireland$q$,$q$Partial$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$For students from outside the EU/EEA, Switzerland and the UK with an offer of admission to a one-year Master's, postgraduate diploma or PhD year at an Irish institution. The 2026 call closed 12 March 2026.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://hea.ie/policy/internationalisation/goi-ies/$q$,$q$EUR 10,000 stipend plus full tuition waiver for the year$q$),
($q$Joint Japan/World Bank Graduate Scholarship Program$q$,$q$World Bank Group with the Government of Japan$q$,$q$Various partner countries$q$,$q$Not stated$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$Ghana is on the list of eligible countries for the 2027 round. Details such as benefits and deadline are on the World Bank scholarships website.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://www.worldbank.org/en/brief/2026/07/15/countries-eligible-for-jjwbgsp-scholarship$q$,$q$Not stated on the page$q$),
($q$India-Africa Maitri Scholarship Scheme$q$,$q$Indian Council for Cultural Relations (ICCR), Government of India$q$,$q$India$q$,$q$Full$q$,$q$Undergraduate and postgraduate$q$,$q$Open to 54 African countries, with 70 slots for Ghana. Covers undergraduate, postgraduate and PhD study in STEM and non-STEM courses (medical, law and integrated courses excluded).$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://iccr.gov.in/academics/scholarships/iccr-scholarship/iccr-scholarship-schemes$q$,$q$Stipend, housing allowance, tuition, return airfare$q$),
($q$NL Scholarship$q$,$q$Dutch government and participating Dutch higher education institutions$q$,$q$Netherlands$q$,$q$Partial$q$,$q$Undergraduate and postgraduate$q$,$q$For non-EEA students applying to a full-time Bachelor's or Master's at a participating Dutch institution who do not already hold a Dutch degree. Apply through the institution's own instructions. The 2027-2028 round is open.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://www.studyinnl.org/finances/nl-scholarship$q$,$q$EUR 5,000 in the first year$q$),
