($q$Danish Government Scholarships for Highly Qualified Non-EU/EEA Students$q$,$q$Danish government (awarded by Danish universities)$q$,$q$Denmark$q$,$q$Partial$q$,$q$Undergraduate and postgraduate$q$,$q$For citizens of countries outside the EU, EEA and Switzerland enrolled in a full degree programme in Denmark. Universities select recipients, so check the admission details of your chosen institution.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://studyindenmark.dk/study-options/scholarships$q$,$q$Full or partial tuition waiver and/or living cost grant$q$),
($q$Global Korea Scholarship (GKS) Graduate Programme$q$,$q$Government of South Korea (NIIED)$q$,$q$South Korea$q$,$q$Full$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$For non-Korean citizens (and non-Korean parents) under 40 with a Bachelor's or Master's degree and a GPA of at least 80 percent. Master's 2 years or doctoral 3 years, after 1 year of Korean language training.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://www.studyinkorea.go.kr/ko/plan/scholarship.do$q$,$q$Airfare, language training, tuition and monthly allowance$q$)
